 "title": "Avignon, 22 June 1400: why the Prior of Portaceli left without leave",
 "caption": "Line 24 of the last page of Benedict XIII's letter to Francesc Climent, read sign by sign with the rebuilt key: \"[he could not come back to us,] as if frightened by the ways of these adversaries of ours who hold us here, and he left in haste without leave\". The clear words around it are Puig's reading, set plain. S. Puig y Puig, Pedro de Luna (1920), p. 475, facsimile of Arxiu Capitular de Barcelona doc. 1068.",
 "unit": "signs",
 "key_note": "Simple substitution, one sign per letter. The letter o is a double loop (ꝏ); c and i share a single small o on the 1920 halftone. Signs are joined by hair-lines with no word breaks; word division here is editorial. One tall stroke in istorum is not accounted for (marked ?). Puig printed 'abique congerio'; the signs give absque.",
